WEBVTT

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.750
Welcome to Resgrid Academy.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.530
In this lesson, we will keep deployment activity and cost evidence together.

00:00:06.949 --> 00:00:11.500
Extended mutual-aid work needs clear personnel, apparatus, dates,

00:00:11.609 --> 00:00:15.109
and cost records that can be reviewed after demobilization.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:18.569
We will explain the features, the setup decisions, and a

00:00:18.569 --> 00:00:20.520
practical way to check the result.

00:00:21.129 --> 00:00:25.689
A strike-team deployment is recorded with its personnel, apparatus and dates.

00:00:26.209 --> 00:00:29.230
Keep deployment records and cost documentation together

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.949
for review and reimbursement.

00:00:31.499 --> 00:00:34.949
The examples in this series use a fictional department and are teaching

00:00:34.949 --> 00:00:37.229
scenarios, not default settings.

00:00:37.889 --> 00:00:39.200
Deployment Finance.

00:00:39.590 --> 00:00:42.289
Deployment records and Deployment Finance.

00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:46.210
Record your next deployment with its personnel and apparatus.

00:00:46.829 --> 00:00:47.790
New Deployment.

00:00:48.219 --> 00:00:49.690
Start a deployment record.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:53.889
Useful when your members deploy to incidents outside your jurisdiction.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:56.399
Deployment From External Order.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:59.920
Create a deployment from a mutual-aid resource order.

00:01:00.329 --> 00:01:03.940
Useful when your members deploy to incidents outside your jurisdiction.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.879
Resource orders describe requested resources and the fills

00:01:07.879 --> 00:01:09.709
departments offer or accept.

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:13.049
Review ordering settings and participating departments.

00:01:13.450 --> 00:01:17.530
Create a fictional request, offer a fill, and review acceptance.

00:01:17.939 --> 00:01:22.590
Reconcile requested quantities, accepted fills, and the remaining resource need.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:25.899
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:01:25.899 --> 00:01:27.379
recording the live workflow.

00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:32.019
An external order records the department fills and their mobilization,

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.139
release, and actual return home.

00:01:34.599 --> 00:01:39.290
Enter an approved sample external order, link its deployment, record the fill

00:01:39.290 --> 00:01:41.320
transitions, and complete closeout.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:43.919
Review dates and resource identity.

00:01:44.369 --> 00:01:48.900
This workspace records manual entry and artifact snapshots; it is not

00:01:48.930 --> 00:01:50.549
an external ordering connector.

00:01:50.949 --> 00:01:53.680
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:55.020
recording the live workflow.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:59.729
Read-only deployment reports bring time entries, supporting artifacts,

00:01:59.809 --> 00:02:01.470
and export outputs together.

00:02:01.949 --> 00:02:05.249
Open a recorded demo deployment and review its time report,

00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.470
summary, and available exports.

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:12.689
Reconcile each time entry with the roster and recorded dates before finance review.

00:02:13.169 --> 00:02:15.960
Confirm availability in the demo department before

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.449
recording the live workflow.

00:02:18.150 --> 00:02:20.830
For the training scenario, work in this order.

00:02:21.300 --> 00:02:21.859
Step 1.

00:02:22.409 --> 00:02:25.949
Create a deployment or start from an external resource order.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:26.979
Step 2.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:31.600
Identify the assigned personnel, apparatus, and operational dates.

00:02:32.019 --> 00:02:32.769
Step 3.

00:02:33.199 --> 00:02:36.709
Record deployment activity and finance documentation for review.

00:02:37.519 --> 00:02:39.060
Now verify the result.

00:02:39.499 --> 00:02:43.259
Reconcile the deployment resources and dates with supporting records.

00:02:43.629 --> 00:02:47.740
Review any daily time and cost documentation required by the workflow.

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:52.200
A common problem to watch for: Deployment Finance is separate from

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.770
the Business Operations add-on.

00:02:54.209 --> 00:02:57.199
A prepared record does not guarantee reimbursement.

00:02:57.809 --> 00:02:59.419
Your practice task is simple.

00:02:59.869 --> 00:03:03.410
Record a two-day demo strike-team deployment and reconcile the

00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:06.740
participating people and units with the supporting documents.

00:03:07.139 --> 00:03:10.939
Record the result, who owns the follow-up, and when it should be reviewed.

